 now",later:"Later",installing:"Updating… the game will reopen by itself"},whatsNew:{title:"Updated to {v} for you",head:"What’s new",ok:"Got it"},versionNotes:{"6.6.0":["Teammates: villagers you rescued now fly in on their own little aircraft, fire a few shots and use a special move: Soup Rain, Lamp Chain, Lantern Bombs, Chime Wave, Wheat Arrows, Tidal Wave, Salt Ward, Broadside and Tide Pool Light","Teammate Bell: when the little bell at the top left completes a turn, a teammate may come to help (two for VIP); the closer you are, the more often they come","Teammates page in the hangar: spend shards on each teammate’s special move, firepower and fly-by boost; give keepsakes to grow your bond through seven heart colors","Keepsakes drop from the weekend dungeon and can be bought with Diamonds in the shop","The Teammate Bell in the hangar is now open: once you have your first teammate, each upgrade brings teammates sooner","Come back often: after 3 days away, your bond fades a little each day, and if it runs out a shadow takes that teammate away until you rescue them again","Combo bell: every 10 combo speeds up the Teammate Bell; when your hull is nearly gone or only one light is left, a teammate rushes in at once","High five: fly into a passing teammate to boost that move, double the buff and grow your bond; they then call a partner over","Duets: two moves cast back to back trigger a combo: Warm Light, Cannonade, Backtide, Sanctuary, Arrow Storm. The Teammates page has a combo book","Bond rewards: at orange and red hearts your teammate writes you a letter; close teammates shout their own line; red hearts earn the titles Kindred Spirit and Heart of the Town","Rescue night: a teammate taken by the shadows is carried in by one; break it to rescue them on the spot and get half your bond back","New weekend dungeon theme Cut Off: fog walls and mirrors block even your teammates; break through with high fives and duets. Double keepsakes","Shop effects upgraded: Noble effects are longer, brighter and have their own flourish, with a live stage in the shop; lucky boxes and Noble effects now have a running gold border"],"6.5.0":["Keep moving: shadows now come from the sky and the sea, and staying put too long invites an ambush; arrows at the screen edge show where they’re coming from","Combo blaze: keep hitting and your bullets burn hotter (gold, blue, white-hot); taking a hit only halves your combo","Embers: defeated shadows may drop one; fly through it for 8 seconds of special shots: Skipping Stone, Boomerang Lamp, Chain Light or Trident Fire","Hull: hits wear it down, and when it’s gone the lighthouse loses a flame; elites spit shadow shots and bosses slam a wide area, so dodge the warnings; fuel can top it up automatically","Helpers: the lighthouse pulses shadows away, lit streetlamps zap house-wreckers, a crosshair lights up when you’re lined up, and after two losses in a row the night gets lighter","From night 15, nine new shadows: Lamp Thief, Ember Eater, Mirror Shade, Fog Weaver and more","Effects in the shop: 6 orbits and 6 trails, each one you collect gives a permanent bonus; a full skin set comes with its own aura","Less grind: sweep, idle rewards and reminders; a “This battle” row on the results, plus new daily tasks, achievements and a Best Combo leaderboard"],"6.4.0":["Ultimates: cooldown halved (20s), and they fire the moment you tap","Bigger text everywhere, easier to read","Clearer alarms when a house or the lighthouse is under attack: red glow, warning sign, bite countdown and a bell","Halloween Night is back to its intended difficulty: no Last Stand in the final wave","More elite shades in later waves and later nights","Tide Harbor: a second town with 4 districts and 4 villagers to rescue; the tide rises and falls","New shades: Surge, Salt and Anchor Shades, plus the Tide Boss","Weather: downpours, storms, hail and cold snaps (bring weather potions)","Hard mode from night 15: reversed controls and four kinds of Silence",